{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"entity framework core entity framework core","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md","fileName":"Entity Framework Core.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Entity Framework Core","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Entity Framework Core Data Modeling]] [[Entity Framework Core Data Access]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Modeling","Entity Framework Core Data Access","Object-Relational Mapping","Database Context","Entity Framework Migration","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"entity framework core entity framework core","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md","fileName":"Entity Framework Core.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Entity Framework Core","heading":"Entity Framework Core","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Entity Framework Core is an open-source [[Object-Relational Mapping|object-relational mapper]] for .NET applications. It lets application code work with domain-specific object classes while mapping their persistent state to a relational database.\n\nAn EF Core model combines entity classes, relationships, conventions, and annotations. A [[Database Context]] coordinates access, a database provider connects the model to a DBMS, and [[Entity Framework Migration|migrations]] translate model changes into schema changes.\n\nIts EF Core chapter brings configuration, querying, change tracking, migrations, direct SQL, and transactions together as one data-layer implementation. The framework is therefore a persistence mechanism behind application boundaries rather than the domain or public API itself.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Modeling","Entity Framework Core Data Access","Object-Relational Mapping","Database Context","Entity Framework Migration","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"entity framework core entity framework core","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Entity Framework Core.md","fileName":"Entity Framework Core.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Entity Framework Core","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]\n\n[[aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf]]\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Modeling","Entity Framework Core Data Access","Object-Relational Mapping","Database Context","Entity Framework Migration","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}